{
  "schema": "moosas.thermal-templates",
  "version": 2,
  "standard": {
    "id": "GB55015-2021",
    "title": "建筑节能与可再生能源利用通用规范",
    "effective_date": "2022-04-01",
    "source_url": "https://ynjn.yn.gov.cn/jnbz/202110/P020261011631961784994.pdf",
    "source_sha256": "7907f68b9c89a2295bab50de3e4f9bdc8479b21db0f31849a87cd293f7fc2829",
    "pages": "Printed pages 4–17: envelope tables; 62–64: Appendix B definitions; 69–77: reference operation",
    "scope": "Normative limits and selected reference conditions only. This library is a simulation scenario, not a building compliance certificate. U includes reference surface films and structural thermal bridges; materials are equivalent homogenized assumptions. Partition/unheated-basement limits are retained for future boundary extensions and are not applied to adiabatic boundaries; entrance doors and balcony panels are outside this adapter scope.",
    "alternate_pdf_url": "https://www.beijing.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengcefagui/qtwj/202204/W020220412578195558564.pdf",
    "publication_url": "https://www.beijing.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengcefagui/qtwj/202204/t20220412_2674410.html",
    "country": "CN"
  },
  "assumptions": {
    "wall": {
      "thermal_mass_j_m2k": 60000,
      "solar_reflectance": 0.3,
      "outside_emissivity": 0.9,
      "inside_emissivity": 0.9
    },
    "slab": {
      "thermal_mass_j_m2k": 120000,
      "solar_reflectance": 0.3,
      "outside_emissivity": 0.9,
      "inside_emissivity": 0.9
    },
    "glass": {
      "thermal_mass_j_m2k": 0,
      "solar_reflectance": 0.4,
      "solar_transmittance": 0.5,
      "outside_emissivity": 0.84,
      "inside_emissivity": 0.84
    },
    "glass_absorptance": 0.1,
    "internal_resistance_m2k_w": 0.2,
    "ground_base_resistance_m2k_w": 0.2,
    "unspecified_ground_insulation_r": 1.0,
    "unspecified_resistance_m2k_w": 1.0,
    "notes": "Capacities are full-construction J/(m2 K), split at shared adiabatic midplanes. Glass is massless; summer equivalent optics use alpha=0.1, tau=max(SHGC_limit-alpha,0), rho=1-SHGC_limit, so tau+alpha<=limit. This does not reproduce a measured glazing product or winter SHGC. Ground insulation R is added to assumed base R; full-floor use of peripheral minimum is a scenario assumption. Unknown table columns use the stricter limit. Default public aliases select class A; select B explicitly only after checking Appendix B area/group-area criteria. Climate aliases select subzone A and do not infer a site climate classification. Residential cooling COP 3.6 outside cold-B/hot-summer reference climates is an engineering extension. Storey count from model levels is an estimate. Normative limits do not prove compliance after explicit model overrides."
  },
